# ============================================================
# Personal Health Graph — .gitignore
# ============================================================
# This file prevents accidental commits of personal health data.
# Template files (_TEMPLATE.md) and README files are tracked.
# User-created data files (dated entries, filled-in profiles) are not.
# ============================================================

# ----- Personal data files (NEVER commit these) -----

# Filled-in state files (contain personal health information)
# These are tracked as blank templates but should not be committed
# once they contain real data. If you're using this repo as your
# working copy (not recommended), uncomment these lines:
# PROFILE.md
# SUPPLEMENTS.md
# PROTOCOLS.md
# DOCTOR_QS.md
# EXPENSES.md
# LABS_HISTORY.md
# GENETICS.md

# Inbox (unprocessed files awaiting intake)
inbox/*
!inbox/README.md

# Dated log entries (symptoms, journal)
symptoms/[0-9]*.md
journal/[0-9]*.md

# Dated integration files (labs, wearables, genetics, etc.)
# Ignore everything in these dirs, then un-ignore README and _TEMPLATE
integrations/labs/*.md
integrations/genetics/*.md
integrations/wearable_daily/*.md
integrations/healthkit/*.md
integrations/microbiome/*.md
integrations/imaging/*.md
integrations/assessments/*.md
integrations/cycle/*.md
!integrations/*/README.md
!integrations/*/_TEMPLATE.md

# Raw data exports (often large, always personal)
integrations/raw/**/*.pdf
integrations/raw/**/*.csv
integrations/raw/**/*.json
integrations/raw/**/*.txt
integrations/raw/**/*.vcf
integrations/raw/**/*.bam
integrations/raw/**/*.gz
integrations/raw/**/*.zip

# Generated reports (contain personal analysis)
# All report files are ignored except the README
reports/*
!reports/README.md

# ----- OS and editor files -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ----- Environment and secrets -----
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
# Personal reference docs (not part of the public template)
GITHUB_SETUP_GUIDE.md
